# SPARQL translation of CQ2-1 — Phase 2
# "Agreements recorded at a given meeting under a given agenda item"
#
# Realization note: the released RDF materializes each Neo4j node that carried
# both the Agreement and Resolution labels as two IRIs sharing one
# spectra:resolutionId. The Agreement IRI carries the decision content; the
# Resolution IRI carries the process placement (madeAt, resolutionBelongsTo).
# The query therefore bridges the two via resolutionId.
#
# Engine note: class membership is asserted via FILTER EXISTS rather than
# positive `?x a <Class>` triple patterns. Greedy join planners (e.g. rdflib)
# order single-variable patterns first, and two class enumerations in one
# basic graph pattern form a cross product (|Resolution| x |Agreement| is
# ~5x10^8 here) before any selective join applies. FILTER EXISTS keeps the
# membership check per-solution. Constants verified against the released
# RAN1-body.ttl.

PREFIX spectra: <https://w3id.org/spectra#>

SELECT ?resolutionId ?content
WHERE {
  ?m spectra:meetingNumber "RAN1#120" .
  ?ai spectra:agendaNumber "9.1.1" .
  ?r spectra:madeAt ?m ;
     spectra:resolutionBelongsTo ?ai ;
     spectra:resolutionId ?resolutionId .
  ?ag spectra:resolutionId ?resolutionId ;
      spectra:content ?content .
  FILTER EXISTS { ?r a spectra:Resolution }
  FILTER EXISTS { ?ag a spectra:Agreement }
}
ORDER BY ?resolutionId
